=== RESOURCE CLIMB: how high can a primitive 13-set block the band ladder? ===
   K = target ceiling (block all shells q<=K).  band-k ceiling = (k+1)*14-1.
   For each K: can we block all q<=K? with what dominance ratio rho=max/2nd?
   rho > 13 => B'-DOMINANT (THM-398 Cor B2 fires => loose anyway).

    K  band  blocked?  min-dominance-rho  non-dom-blocker?  maxentry  true-height
    27  ~ 2   YES       rho=  1.00          YES          476     29
    41  ~ 3   YES       rho=  1.00          YES          726     43
    55  ~ 4   YES       rho=  1.05          YES          989     56
    69  ~ 5   no(res=26)   --                  --              1189     best-effort
    83  ~ 6   no(res=74)   --                  --              1406     best-effort

=== verdict ===
   NON-DOMINANT blockers found at K = [27, 41, 55]
   dominance rho vs K (does rho -> 13 as K grows? => forced dominance):
      K=27: min non-dom rho achievable = 1.00, true height = 29, max entry 476
      K=41: min non-dom rho achievable = 1.00, true height = 43, max entry 726
      K=55: min non-dom rho achievable = 1.05, true height = 56, max entry 989
   HIGHEST K with a NON-DOMINANT full blocker = 55 (band-4); ladder height there > 55.
   => the band ladder has NO finite ceiling for non-dominant configs at least up
      to band-4; consistent with HYP-2438 (closure needs B'(any)).

=== TOTAL 405.3s ===
